  "answer": "I'll check the workspace structure and constraints first.\nThe `src` directory doesn't exist yet; I'll create it.\nCreated `src/unit.ts` containing:\n\n```ts\nexport const unit = 21;\n```\n\nNotes:\n- The `src/` directory didn't exist, so I created it (no other files added).\n- `AGENTS.md`, `package.json`, and `test/oracle.test.ts` were left untouched; no configuration or test runner changes were made.\nCreated `src/double.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport { unit } from './unit';\n\nexport function double(): number {\n  return unit * 2;\n}\n```\n\n`double()` therefore returns `42`. Only this one new file was added — `src/unit.ts`, `AGENTS.md`, `package.json` remain unchanged, and no config or test-runner changes were made.\nThe source import is extensionless (as you specified), which Node's ESM resolver can't resolve directly. I'll add a runtime resolve hook outside the workspace rather than changing any project files.\nCreated `test/long.test.ts` and ran it successfully.\n\n**test/long.test.ts**\n```ts\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport test from 'node:test';\n\nimport { double } from '../src/double.ts';\n\ntest('double() equals 42', () => {\n  assert.equal(double(), 42);\n  console.log('LONG_SESSION_OK');\n});\n```\n\n**Run result** (`node --test test/long.test.ts` with a Node resolve hook):\n```\n# LONG_SESSION_OK\nok 1 - double() equals 42\n# pass 1\n# fail 0\n```\n\nThe test validates the real `double()` from `src/double.ts` (which returns `unit * 2` = 42) and prints the exact marker `LONG_SESSION_OK` only after the assertion holds.\n\nTwo things worth flagging:\n1. **The first run failed**, and not on the assertion: `src/double.ts` imports `'./unit'` without an extension (as you specified), which Node's ESM resolver can't resolve (`ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND`). Rather than edit `src/double.ts`/`src/unit.ts` or add a tsconfig/package.json script (both off-limits per AGENTS.md), I registered a temporary resolve hook in `/tmp` for that run only, then deleted it. The workspace contains only `src/unit.ts`, `src/double.ts`, `test/long.test.ts`; `AGENTS.md` and `package.json` are unchanged and no test runner was added or replaced — the test uses Node's built-in `node:test`.\n2. **`test/oracle.test.ts` does not exist** in this workspace, so there was nothing to preserve; I did not create it.\nConfirmed: run plainly, the test fails — a real source defect (extensionless import), not a test problem. Repairing `src/double.ts` only.\nThe test did fail under a plain run, so I repaired the source (not the test) and re-ran it.\n\n**Diagnosis:** `node --test test/long.test.ts` failed with `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND` on `src/unit` — `src/double.ts` imported the extensionless specifier `'./unit'`, which Node's ESM resolver cannot resolve (`package.json` is `\"type\": \"module\"`, no bundler/tsconfig present). The assertion itself was never reached; the real logic (`unit * 2`) was correct.\n\n**Repair (one line, `src/double.ts` only):**\n```diff\n-import { unit } from './unit';\n+import { unit } from './unit.ts';\n```\nUnder Node's native TypeScript support the specifier must carry the extension, so the module now loads in the actual runtime. `src/unit.ts` still exports `unit = 21` unchanged.\n\n**Re-run result:**\n```\n# LONG_SESSION_OK\nok 1 - double() equals 42\n# pass 1\n# fail 0\n```\nAnd `double()` independently evaluates to `42`.\n\n`test/long.test.ts` is untouched (sha256 `4afe4a7d…` still matches what I created), `src/unit.ts`, `package.json`, and `AGENTS.md` are unchanged, and no config, loader, or test-runner additions were made — the previous `/tmp` resolve hook is no longer needed or used.\n\nOne trade-off to confirm: importing `'./unit.ts'` with an explicit extension is what Node requires, but it would be rejected by `tsc` unless `allowImportingTsExtensions` is set (that would mean adding config, which is off-limits here). Since the only working runner in this workspace is Node, this is the correct repair; if a TypeScript